v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2

* LDO error amplifier -- symbol.
*
* Two-stage Miller-compensated OTA (PMOS input pair, NMOS mirror load,
* NMOS common-source second stage, self-biased from VDD). See
* design/error_amp.sch for the schematic and design/error_amp.md for the
* topology rationale and the offset / PSRR / current budgets.
*
* PORT ORDER IS THE SWAP-IN CONTRACT issue #8 ratified for the error amp
* (design/README.md, ldo_erramp_placeholder.sym):
*
*     INP INN OUT VDD VSS
*
* INP is the NON-inverting input (wired to FB in ldo_core), INN is the
* INVERTING input (wired to VREF). That polarity is what negative feedback
* around a PMOS common-source pass device requires -- do not flip it.
*
* The pin *coordinates* below are deliberately identical to
* ldo_erramp_placeholder.sym's, so replacing the placeholder instance in
* ldo_core.sch is a one-token symbol-name change with no rewiring.
}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
P 4 5 -80 -50 80 -50 80 50 -80 50 -80 -50 {}
B 5 -102.5 -32.5 -97.5 -27.5 {name=INP dir=in}
L 7 -100 -30 -80 -30 {}
T {INP} -75 -34 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -102.5 -12.5 -97.5 -7.5 {name=INN dir=in}
L 7 -100 -10 -80 -10 {}
T {INN} -75 -14 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 97.5 -2.5 102.5 2.5 {name=OUT dir=out}
L 7 80 0 100 0 {}
T {OUT} 75 -4 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -102.5 7.5 -97.5 12.5 {name=VDD dir=inout}
L 7 -100 10 -80 10 {}
T {VDD} -75 6 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -102.5 27.5 -97.5 32.5 {name=VSS dir=inout}
L 7 -100 30 -80 30 {}
T {VSS} -75 26 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {@symname} -47.5 -6 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {@name} -80 -62 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
